WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.030
Hello there, my children.

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:07.560
It’s me, SCP-343, but you probably know
me better as God.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.790
It’s been strange lately, hasn’t it?

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:14.380
To the untrained eye, it seems like things
are only getting crazier out there.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.880
Nothing seems certain or safe anymore.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.380
So naturally, you’ve got questions for me.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:23.099
It makes sense, in your position I’d probably
do the same thing.

00:00:23.099 --> 00:00:28.060
So let’s see what burning queries are on
your mind, and of course, I’ll do my best

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.320
to answer them.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:36.360
Indigo Wolf said, “I’d ask him for instructions:
“What’s the best way to raise SCP-999

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.430
to be ready for the Scarlet King?”

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:40.550
So we’d be fully prepared for his arrival.”

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:44.690
Ah, the Scarlet King, he’s a nasty customer.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:47.640
I try to avoid associating with him when I
can.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:53.140
His vibes are atrocious, and he certainly
has some unpleasant plans for everything I’ve

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.780
created if ever he gets his way.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.460
But to answer your question about how best
to raise SCP-999.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:02.450
To me, the answer is obvious: With love.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:08.210
The Scarlet King is the master of malice and
savagery, and therefore, malice and savagery

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:11.259
cannot be used as tools against him.

00:01:11.259 --> 00:01:15.689
Only the light of love can burn out the hate
hiding in the dark.

00:01:15.689 --> 00:01:24.119
Tyron Morgan said, “I’d ask, Why does
he choose to be at an SCP Foundation site

00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:27.229
rather than in the world helping people?”

00:01:27.229 --> 00:01:32.040
There are many ways to help, and not all of
them mean getting involved directly.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:36.579
A set of training wheels can help someone
ride a bike, but they will never truly know

00:01:36.579 --> 00:01:39.509
how to ride until the training wheels are
removed.

00:01:39.509 --> 00:01:41.840
What’s that saying you came up with?

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.329
The Lord helps those who help themselves.

00:01:45.329 --> 00:01:51.700
Clockworksnowman said, “I would ask him
something about how he said "it's not one

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:57.359
of mine" when asked about 682 and then WHO
did make it).”

00:01:57.359 --> 00:02:03.039
There are certain details I’d rather not
get into when discussing that...thing, but

00:02:03.039 --> 00:02:07.509
all I can tell you is, whoever made it didn’t
make it with love.

00:02:07.509 --> 00:02:10.240
Beasts like that are perversions of the gift
of creation.

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:12.390
It doesn’t even enjoy its own life.

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:14.569
Is that any way to exist?

00:02:14.569 --> 00:02:17.220
We must pity it if anything.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:22.400
Noct_28 Hi said, “I guess an interesting
question would be “What do you think of

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.849
Atheists?”

00:02:24.849 --> 00:02:25.860
Depends on the atheist.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:30.680
I’ve known Angelic Atheists and Monstrous
Believers, and of course, vice versa.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:36.069
What matters most in life is that you’re
a good person - that you’re kind and understanding

00:02:36.069 --> 00:02:41.489
to your fellow human beings, and you leave
the world a little better than you found it.

00:02:41.489 --> 00:02:46.720
Even if you don’t believe in me, if you’re
a good person, I’ll believe in you.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:54.769
Chase Crowe said, “Are there any regrets
that you have, in terms of what your creation

00:02:54.769 --> 00:02:56.209
has become?”

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:57.310
Regret.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.560
It’s an interesting word.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:05.890
The Greek playwright Agathon once said, “Only
this is denied even to God, The power to make

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:08.140
what has been done undone.”

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:13.030
I regret nothing of my past because the past
is beyond all of us.

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:17.110
For what it’s worth, I’m proud of all
of you.

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:24.531
Irish Spartan Studios said, “I'd ask him:
"When will the 'Surviving Infinite Ikea' video

00:03:24.531 --> 00:03:25.531
come out?"

00:03:25.531 --> 00:03:27.719
It already has, my son.

00:03:27.719 --> 00:03:28.719
You see?

00:03:28.719 --> 00:03:29.840
Patience is a virtue.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:36.360
Max’s Intense Videos said, “Is there a
way to terminate the immortal lizard or at

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:40.550
the very least make him not want to kill every
living thing?”

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:46.680
I’ve gone on record saying this before,
but that thing isn’t one of mine.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:50.410
The SCP Foundation will have to figure out
that nasty piece of work by themselves.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:56.160
Dr. Veronica said, “I'd ask him "What's
the name of the SCP doctor we see in all these

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:59.290
videos with black hair, a black beard, and
glasses?

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:03.890
He's the one presenting anomalies to us more
than anybody else, so he must be important."

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:05.739
He’s a charming fellow.

00:04:05.739 --> 00:04:09.239
We hang out every Wednesday and watch episodes
of Ru Paul’s Drag Race on Netflix.

00:04:09.239 --> 00:04:13.720
I won’t share his name here out of respect
for his privacy, but rest assured, you’re

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:18.049
in good hands with him.

00:04:18.049 --> 00:04:27.900
Brandon Kaminari said, "Considering the Foundation's
tendencies and devotion to their cause, other

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:34.030
than the times you felt a Divine Duty to Intervene,
have you ever tried to convince the Foundation

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:41.120
to cure something or someone, offer to completely
destroy an item, or even make their work easier?"

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.950
Frankly, that isn’t my place.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:48.419
The problem with ultimate power is that it
means you can’t really choose sides.

00:04:48.419 --> 00:04:53.870
To put my finger on the scale could lead to
catastrophic effects, and if I save one person

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:58.710
or even a handful of people, that means I’d
need to save everyone all the time.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:02.900
And if I’m always saving everyone, you no
longer have free will.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:09.849
Mangolad said, “I would ask him: "Is there
any meaning to all the suffering and insanity

00:05:09.849 --> 00:05:11.560
we face everyday?

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:18.430
Do we matter on the grand scheme of things,
or are we just pebbles on a road?"

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:20.420
Suffering has no inherent meaning.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.220
In fact, nothing does.

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:26.830
But the beauty of that is that you get to
choose your own meaning.

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:31.400
Suffering can weaken or strengthen you, it
only depends on the lessons you choose to

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:32.530
take from it.

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:34.460
And of course, you matter.

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:39.310
In fact, you’re made of matter, just like
everything else.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:41.960
The meaning of that is up to you.

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:47.710
Ockinho said, “I would ask him about the
disease that SCP-049 is trying to cure.”

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:48.710
The Pestilence?

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:51.100
He always was a neat freak, that one.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:55.710
I can’t say I know what he’s obsessed
with, but I can only hope that the SCP Foundation

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:58.389
someday cures him of his germaphobia.

00:05:58.389 --> 00:06:03.979
Krizia said, “As much as I'd love to ask
him about other SCPs or deep existential questions,

00:06:03.979 --> 00:06:07.740
I would rather just chill peacefully with
him while we eat hamburgers.”

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:11.020
That certainly sounds like a pleasant afternoon
to me.

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:13.660
You should swing by again sometime, and we’ll
hang out.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:20.319
Especially if you buy the hamburgers.

00:06:20.319 --> 00:06:25.940
Speedy Lurchix said, “I think my question
would be: "How can you still be so kind in

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:27.970
the face of the cruelty on this planet?

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:31.630
How come you don't become bitter or desperate
or angry?"

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:35.099
Nobody’s perfect, not even me.

00:06:35.099 --> 00:06:40.639
There are certainly times that I do feel desperate,
bitter, and angry, but what’s important

00:06:40.639 --> 00:06:45.330
to remember is that this doesn’t have to
stop you from being kind.

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:50.009
In a cruel world, you can choose to either
be a part of the cruelty or be one of the

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:52.599
brave people standing against it.

00:06:52.599 --> 00:06:59.229
Don’t feel bad for being angry - let it
pass, pick yourself back up, and carry on

00:06:59.229 --> 00:07:00.569
with a smile.

00:07:00.569 --> 00:07:08.690
Ken V said, “I would ask him if there is
any SCP that he fears and/or is unwilling

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:11.110
to approach for any particular reason.”

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:15.919
There’s no SCP I won’t approach, but there
are definitely some I don’t like having

00:07:15.919 --> 00:07:16.919
in my company.

00:07:16.919 --> 00:07:20.229
Have you seen that slimy old man from cell
106?

00:07:20.229 --> 00:07:22.570
Incredibly unpleasant fellow.

00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:28.580
Antonio Ricardo Moncada Osorio said, “Can
I have a big chocolate bar?”

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:32.449
That’s the question I would ask before probably
thinking up something existential.”

00:07:32.449 --> 00:07:38.860
Well, that all depends on your answer to my
next question: What’s your favorite kind

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:40.360
of chocolate?

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:44.949
Daniel Flores said, “Ever since I read about
him, I actually have always wanted to sit

00:07:44.949 --> 00:07:46.610
and play chess with him.

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:48.159
No better practice than GOD.”

00:07:48.159 --> 00:07:51.229
Well, you know what they say: Failure is the
best teacher.

00:07:51.229 --> 00:07:57.879
And if you play chess with me, you’re sure
to receive it.

00:07:57.879 --> 00:08:02.120
Certain Words said, “A simple question.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.129
“What is my purpose?”

00:08:04.129 --> 00:08:07.349
Just so I can rest easy, with my end destination
known.”

00:08:07.349 --> 00:08:13.229
Your purpose is to use your enthusiasm and
your skills to make yourself happy and make

00:08:13.229 --> 00:08:14.849
the world a better place.

00:08:14.849 --> 00:08:17.759
How exactly you do that is up to you, kid.

00:08:17.759 --> 00:08:18.759
Good luck.

00:08:18.759 --> 00:08:23.820
Christina Jones said, "How can I live forever?"

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:28.889
Then I would spend the rest of our day talking
about distant galaxies and theoretical physics.”

00:08:28.889 --> 00:08:32.220
You don’t want to live forever, Christina.

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:36.800
Life seems awfully short to happy people because
time flies when you’re having fun.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.710
Conversely, you won’t find anything duller
than eternity.

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:44.470
However, I’ll definitely take you up on
the distant galaxies and theoretical physics.

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:51.110
LizzyLizENDton said, “Honestly I would just
ask “God” why he let the world go to hell.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:55.310
I’m a Christian and I know God believes
in free will and letting the world do it’s

00:08:55.310 --> 00:09:00.570
own thing but sometimes I really wonder why
He would let some of the bad happen to good

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.620
people, or happen in general.”

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:07.720
It’s a tragedy, really, the Problem of Evil.

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:10.620
Why do the good suffer while the bad prosper?

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:12.420
Why does cruelty exist?

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:15.850
Why are some fortunate and others seem doomed
from birth?

00:09:15.850 --> 00:09:21.590
Evil is the dark residue of free will, the
ability for one to choose their path in life.

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:27.400
It hurts, and my heart aches for its victims,
but without choice, there would be no evil

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.829
and no good.

00:09:28.829 --> 00:09:33.339
You’d cease to even be human, and I could
never do that to you.

00:09:33.339 --> 00:09:36.550
Royal Frostie said, “I would ask him on
a date.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:38.390
Having the ultimate SCP boyfriend.”

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:45.230
I’m flattered by the sentiment, but I see
you all as my children, so I’d hate to make

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:46.230
it weird.

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:50.910
El-Squishi said, “I'd want to ask him simply,
if I'm doing okay so far in life.

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:54.779
Oh, and ask if he has any good recipes, I
bet he does!”

00:09:54.779 --> 00:09:56.230
You’re doing just fine.

00:09:56.230 --> 00:10:00.640
And as long as you keep love in your heart,
and do everything you do with the goal of

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:05.360
bettering this world for yourself and others,
you’ll continue to do splendidly.

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:08.250
And yes, I know many good recipes.

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:12.010
I owe it to my voracious reading of Anthony
Bourdain’s books, me-rest-his-soul.

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:18.970
Gilda said, "God, why am I so deeply miserable
and unable to enjoy or do anything of importance

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:21.529
anymore?"

00:10:21.529 --> 00:10:23.290
You might have depression.

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:27.589
Speak to some friends and loved ones about
this, and see a therapist if possible.

00:10:27.589 --> 00:10:30.550
I love you, and you’re not alone.

00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:33.710
Just keep going and I believe in you.

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:39.779
Merdop said, “With him being the all powerful
creator of the universe, I would of course

00:10:39.779 --> 00:10:43.709
ask him “What’s the deal with airline
food?”

00:10:43.709 --> 00:10:51.040
The altitude, high decibel level, and stale
air of a plane environment weaken your ability

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:56.139
to register salty and sweet tastes, causing
food consumed on a plane to appear more bland

00:10:56.139 --> 00:10:59.260
and flavorless than food consumed while on
the ground.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:03.290
Hope that clears it up for you, my child.

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:10.170
PyroTechy said, “I'd ask to be granted his
powers for a day, just to see from his perspective,

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:12.279
though I might be terminated after…”

00:11:12.279 --> 00:11:17.310
There’s a delightful Jim Carrey film called
Bruce Almighty about why this desire isn’t

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:18.850
what it’s cracked up to be.

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:24.620
I can safely say that Morgan Freeman also
does a wonderful job representing yours truly.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:30.480
Alexander Berry said, "Is my fate already
determined or am I able to choose mine?"

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:33.410
It’s as determined as you want it to be,
Alexander.

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:38.590
If you give yourself in and refuse to make
your own choices, then your fate ceases to

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:40.380
be yours to control.

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:45.840
But if you choose, and fight for your choice,
then your fate is all your own.

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:50.100
Decade Gaming said, “I would tell him to
give me infinite pizza.”

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:56.800
That may be a waste of my divine powers, when
SCP-458, the Never-Ending Pizza Box, exists.

00:11:56.800 --> 00:12:03.380
The Gaming Bear said, “I would ask where
you could find the best hamburger.”

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:07.590
There are plenty of decent places to get a
hamburger on this fine earth, but personally,

00:12:07.590 --> 00:12:11.150
I’m a fan of Five Guys.

00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:13.490
Game Falor said, “Does Satan exist?”

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:14.490
Satan?

00:12:14.490 --> 00:12:19.279
In the sense of a being who exists to tempt
the weaker members of mankind to evil and

00:12:19.279 --> 00:12:20.279
corruption?

00:12:20.279 --> 00:12:22.910
Let me tell you, my child: Those people don’t
need the help.

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:29.880
Henry Galley said, “I have a question for
God: WHY!?”

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:34.290
I’m afraid that’s one you’re going to
need to figure out yourself.

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:37.610
Thank you for all the questions, they’ve
given me a lot to ponder.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:42.529
Take it from your creator: Life is a lot more
interesting when you’re curious, so never

00:12:42.529 --> 00:12:44.970
let the world beat that out of you.

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:49.440
Little disclaimer from the Foundation here:
Whether this particular anomaly is actually

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:54.660
God himself, or simply a very powerful reality
warper, it’s a distinction we’re not fully

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:56.089
comfortable making.

00:12:56.089 --> 00:12:59.860
Perhaps taking his words with a little pinch
of salt...

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:04.570
Now go check out “SCP-096 - Look at a Picture
of Shy Guy in Space?

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:10.000
The Shy Guy Questions and Theories” and
“SCP-049 - What Actually is the Pestilence?

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:14.290
The Plague Doctor Questions and Theories”,
and keep an eye on our community tab for more

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:16.380
chances to take part in a video like this
one!

